// special attributes definition
// _type
	// can be any of the following: "type", "string", "integer", "bool", "email", "password" or any other previously declared type
// _write
	// can be one of the following: no, yes, once 
// _attribute
	// can be a name of any attribute or any other subject
// _mandatory
	// can be any of the following: true, false, 0, 1
// _plural
	// can be 0,  the maximum number of elements of this kind or true which means inifinity   
// _hidden
	// can be 0, or expression   
// _default
	// can be one of the accepted functions as $self(),$timenow(), $next()

// _/_/_/_/_/_/_/_/_/_/_/_/_/_/_/_/_/_/_/_/_/_/_/
// _/
// _/ definition of primitive types
// _/
